  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation is the dominant design choice (+0.092 over singleprofile). However, we have only tested one aggregation method (avgpool) for multiprofile. Question: config_020 isolates the aggregation method (transformer vs avgpool) while holding all other variables constant relative to config_018, directly testing whether a more expressive, attention-based aggregation can better capture inter-profile relationships than simple averaging. Why this is the best next experiment: Aggregation is the mechanism by which the largest observed gain (multiprofile) is realized, so understanding its ceiling is critical. A single-variable change from the current best keeps the comparison clean and maximally informative. If transformer significantly outperforms avgpool, it opens a high-impact direction for subsequent experiments; if not, we can confidently rule out transformer aggregation and redirect budget toward fusion strategy or image encoder upgrades."
